## What Makes It Special\
\
Most code review bots require:\
- External API keys\
- Third-party services\
- Credit cards\
- Configuration\
\
This bot requires:\
\uc0\u9989  Just GitHub (you already have it)\
\uc0\u9989  Just the code (no secrets)\
\uc0\u9989  Just a workflow file (copy/paste)\
\
---\
\
## Example\
\
When you open a PR with this code:\
\
```javascript\
function getUserById(id) \{\
  const query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = " + id;\
  return database.query(query);\
\}\
\
const API_KEY = "sk-1234567890";\
console.log("Debug");\
```\
\
The bot will comment:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec6 \uc0\u55357 \u56628  CRITICAL SQL Injection vulnerability detected. User input is concatenated directly into SQL query.\
Suggestion: Use parameterized queries db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id])\
Why? Concatenating user input allows attackers to execute arbitrary SQL.\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf2 \strokec7 \
